body:
MMR-57 working note (16:26 UTC). The confirming clean-install sequence's first rerun passed install, disable, remove and reload. Its read-only phase was invalid: icacls adds SYNCHRONIZE to every deny entry, even one of listed rights (`(DENY)(W,D,DC)` came out as `DeleteSubdirectoriesAndFiles, Write, Delete, Synchronize`), and a denied SYNCHRONIZE fails every open. The game stopped right after the module's descriptor was listed, before the probe ran. The same cause explains the first sequence's read-only stall. Fixed in `tools/Test-CleanInstall.ps1`:
- the denial is set through .NET `FileSystemAccessRule` (no SYNCHRONIZE; reproduced on a scratch folder: reads and listing work, while create, modify, mkdir and delete are refused);
- the read-only probe runs only when the access check proves that;
- a missing probe result is recorded instead of aborting the sequence.

The whole sequence is rerunning.
